precincts/42127.json","bytes":51469,"precincts":35},{"id":"42129","name":"Westmoreland County","bbox":[-79.90495,40.04035,-78.97381,40.68005],"file":"precincts/42129.json","bytes":346867,"precincts":309},{"id":"42131","name":"Wyoming County","bbox":[-76.2831,41.37652,-75.71851,41.65183],"file":"precincts/42131.json","bytes":28329,"precincts":28},{"id":"42133","name":"York County","bbox":[-77.13742,39.7198,-76.23869,40.22633],"file":"precincts/42133.json","bytes":221102,"precincts":163}],"layers":[{"kind":"state","file":"layers/state.json","bytes":7793,"shapes":1,"good_to_zoom":10.1},{"kind":"county","file":"layers/county.json","bytes":59614,"shapes":67,"good_to_zoom":10.1},{"kind":"cd","file":"layers/cd.json","bytes":35057,"shapes":17,"good_to_zoom":10.1},{"kind":"senate","file":"layers/senate.json","bytes":60539,"shapes":50,"good_to_zoom":10.1},{"kind":"house","file":"layers/house.json","bytes":155793,"shapes":203,"good_to_zoom":10.1},{"kind":"mcd","file":"layers/mcd.json","bytes":1333194,"shapes":2560,"good_to_zoom":11.8},{"kind":"ward","file":"layers/ward.json","bytes":523057,"shapes":1220,"good_to_zoom":11.8},{"kind":"school","file":"layers/school.json","bytes":430063,"shapes":500,"good_to_zoom":11.8}],"school":{"files":"school/<id>.json"},"notes":{"lines":"Every precinct, county, municipal, ward, legislative and congressional line is a 2020 census block's, generalised by at most 1.5 metres and set on a grid of 0.00001 degree (about a metre). A point within a few metres of a line can fall on either side of it.","precincts":"Pennsylvania publishes no statewide map of its election districts as they stand in 2026. Each shape here is one of the Legislative Reapportionment Commission's 2021 voting districts (the Census Bureau's 2020 voting districts brought up to date with the counties in 2021), cut wherever a 2022 House, Senate or congressional line crosses it, and named as the Commission names it. Counties have split, merged or renumbered some election districts since (of the 9,016 in the Department of State's 2024 returns, 8,416 carry a 2021 code): the county board of elections is the authority. What a ballot depends on (county, municipality, ward, House, Senate and congressional district) is put together from whole census blocks under the plans in force and does not depend on the precinct.","districts":"The House and Senate districts are the Legislative Reapportionment Commission's 2022 Final Plan and the congressional districts the plan the Supreme Court of Pennsylvania adopted in Carter v. Chapman (February 23, 2022): the lines used in 2022 and 2024 and in force for 2026. The Commission's block files and the Census Bureau's equivalency files give every block the same district.","municipalities":"Every borough, township, city and town (the Census Bureau's county subdivisions); a precinct's municipality is its blocks' own. Pennsylvania elects its municipal offices in odd-numbered years, so no municipal contest is on this ballot.","wards":"A ward is drawn where the Commission's voting district names one (a city's or borough's ward); some wards hold several precincts.","school":"School district lines are the Census Bureau's 2025 file. Which districts a precinct lies in is analysis, not an official list: a district counts when its part of the precinct is at least 60 metres thick somewhere; school_pct is each district's share of the precinct (land and water, not voters). School directors are elected in odd-numbered years.","courts":"Judges of the courts of common pleas and magisterial district judges are elected in odd-numbered years; no judicial district is drawn.","polling":"Polling places are the Department of State's list for November 3, 2026; see polling_places.json for how its precincts were matched to these shapes, and its status.","authority":"For which election district an address is in, and where to vote, the county board of elections and the Department of State's polling place finder are the authority.","precinct_ids":"A precinct's id is its county's five digits, a full stop and the Commission's six-character voting district code (42003.000170); a voting district cut by a district line has .p and the piece's number after it (42029.000010.p2)."},"sources":[{"id":"pa-lrc-2021-geography","agency":"Pennsylvania Legislative Reapportionment Commission","title":"2021 LRC Data Release 2 - Geography (WP_Blocks, WP_VotingDistricts, WP_Municipalities)","about":"The 2020 census blocks and the Commission's 2021 voting districts: the Census Bureau's 2020 voting districts adjusted by the Commission to the most recent precinct boundaries the counties reported (released October 2021, certified by Resolution 6A). Every line of the map's precincts, counties, municipalities, wards and legislative and congressional districts is a block's. Population columns are never read.","url":"https://www.redistricting.state.pa.us/maps/","file":"https://www.redistricting.state.pa.us/resources/GISData/Census/2021/2021-DataSet2-WithPrisoner/LRC%20Data%20Release%202%20-%20Geography.zip","fetched":"2026-10-17","bytes":342798402,"sha256":"c0d245b2e5f812f18a0cc92bf1103e0fe0bdd18956946267eae0c12e82f5d853","rows":337039,"voting_districts":9178,"vintage":"2021"},{"id":"pa-lrc-2022-house-final","agency":"Pennsylvania Legislative Reapportionment Commission","title":"2022 LRC-House-Final.csv: the 2022 Final Plan, State House, block by block","about":"Which of the 203 House districts each block is in: the plan filed February 4, 2022, in force for the 2022, 2024 and 2026 elections. The Census Bureau's 2024 State Legislative District Block Equivalency File gives every block the same district.","url":"https://www.redistricting.state.pa.us/maps/","file":"https://www.redistricting.state.pa.us/Resources/GISData/Districts/Legislative/House/2021-Final/CSV/2022%20LRC-House-Final.csv","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"17e11f451196cf0b6253c01386592426f867949b76b189c084f04bbf24a92e15","rows":337039},{"id":"pa-lrc-2022-senate-final","agency":"Pennsylvania Legislative Reapportionment Commission","title":"2022 LRC Senate Final.csv: the 2022 Final Plan, State Senate, block by block","about":"Which of the 50 Senate districts each block is in (the odd-numbered seats are on the 2026 ballot). The Census Bureau's 2024 file gives every block the same district.","url":"https://www.redistricting.state.pa.us/maps/","file":"https://www.redistricting.state.pa.us/Resources/GISData/Districts/Legislative/Senate/2021-Final/CSV/2022%20LRC%20Senate%20Final.csv","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"ff7a79d2da3df2094bebe9ab0f19d91bc2bfec8537f8d07a034b6b0d1b3dfbef","rows":337039},{"id":"pa-lrc-carter-plan-2022","agency":"Pennsylvania Legislative Reapportionment Commission","title":"2022-02-25 Carter-adjusted: the congressional plan the Supreme Court of Pennsylvania adopted (Carter v. Chapman), block by block","about":"Which of the 17 congressional districts each block is in, under the plan adopted February 23, 2022, in force for 2026. The Census Bureau's 119th Congress Block Equivalency File gives every block the same district.","url":"https://www.redistricting.state.pa.us/maps/","file":"https://www.redistricting.state.pa.us/Resources/GISData/Districts/Congressional/2021/CSV/2022-02-25%20Carter-adjusted.csv","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"d90c735a2cbf73f7b2f203d8a8e2459f575f2ca29cd8a2dfe75e27363eae9db6","rows":337039},{"id":"pa-census-bef-2024-cd119","agency":"U.S. Census Bureau","title":"2024 State Legislative District and 119th Congressional District Block Equivalency Files (sldl24.zip, sldu24.zip, cd119.zip)","about":"Read only to check the Commission's block files: every Pennsylvania block is in the same district in both.","url":"https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/decennial/rdo/mapping-files/2025/2024-state-legislative-bef/sldl24.zip","upper_url":"https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/decennial/rdo/mapping-files/2025/2024-state-legislative-bef/sldu24.zip","cd_url":"https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/decennial/rdo/mapping-files/2025/119-congressional-district-befs/cd119.zip","sha256":"0d916eb6f901a891014a881ac951de40148f2ce391a275fe86ff172d47cada13","upper_sha256":"52e4d2b1ebdf8470d906c8de9b2824fa86f936e8c016ce9b5598fb2b7271b55d","cd_sha256":"1433feb5178dc7b4188ee30f5f7f715851f4400740b8fe1ce606a876c6294bd6"},{"id":"pa-census-tiger-2025-cousub","agency":"U.S. Census Bureau","title":"TIGER/Line Shapefiles 2025, county subdivisions, Pennsylvania (tl_2025_42_cousub.zip)","about":"Municipality names, and the county areas the blocks are checked against.","url":"https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/TIGER2025/COUSUB/tl_2025_42_cousub.zip","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"f07025c53f4192bc0c81c457930f8d6051ac7b5dad1945dd2ef042e6510b8bc8","rows":2572},{"id":"pa-census-tiger-2025-unsd","agency":"U.S. Census Bureau","title":"TIGER/Line Shapefiles 2025, unified school districts, Pennsylvania (tl_2025_42_unsd.zip)","about":"School district lines as the Bureau had them for the 2024-25 school year.","url":"https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/TIGER2025/UNSD/tl_2025_42_unsd.zip","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"2ab52ae845065c2a6a69127ba595e4e8b7249c2626e2c2c6c3da9bceb201e619","rows":500},{"id":"pa-dos-polling-places-2026-11-03","agency":"Pennsylvania Department of State (published on the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania's ArcGIS organization, PennMap)","title":"PP_SEPT_18_2026_FINAL_092526: Polling Places of Pennsylvania for the elections of November 3, 2026","url":"https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=51cdd076b44f457894c09dc5dcfb5daf","service":"https://services3.arcgis.com/dBSpWiMm4bd648G0/arcgis/rest/services/PP_SEPT_18_2026_FINAL_092526/FeatureServer/0"}]}